    "body": "Adds ADR-017, which decides to implement `display: none` and retire the hardcoded skip list in `layout.cpp`.\n\n## The gap this fixes\n\nSince PR #110 (ADR-011), `layout.cpp` has a hardcoded helper that skips seven tags during layout:\n\n- `head`, `style`, `script`, `title`, `meta`, `link`, `base`\n\nIt works, but it has three problems:\n\n- **Not overridable by author CSS.** `<head style=\"display: block\">` cannot render, because the C++ helper fires before cascade ever applies.\n- **Magic special case.** Future contributors have to learn about this list before touching `layout_element`.\n- **Redundant with the `Display` enum.** ADR-016 added `Display::None` but never wired it in.\n\n## The decision\n\n1. **`layout_element` skips `Display::None` children** — both in the block-child path and in the inline-run collection path.\n2. **UA stylesheet gets 8 rules**: `head, style, script, title, meta, link, base, template { display: none }`. `template` is added beyond the current skip list because per HTML5 it does not render.\n3. **Delete `is_non_rendered_tag`** from `layout.cpp`.\n\nThe skip now comes from cascade (which is where `display` belongs per CSS 2.1) rather than from C++.\n\n## Two behavior changes\n\n**Author override becomes possible.** `<head style=\"display: block\">` now renders, where before it was force-skipped. Rare in practice but spec-compliant.\n\n**Skip semantic matches CSS 2.1.** `display: none` removes the element and its subtree from the formatting structure entirely. Author CSS `div { display: none }` now works for any element, not just the 7 in the helper.\n\n## Why this is small\n\n- ~10 lines of `layout.cpp` change\n- ~2 lines of UA stylesheet\n- ~1 line of existing test updates\n- ~10 lines of new tests\n\nCompare to ADR-016's ~1500 lines. This ADR closes a gap rather than opening a new one.\n\n## Deferred\n\n`display: flex`, `display: grid`, `display: table` — different layout modes.\n\n`display: contents` — element produces no box, its children participate in parent's formatting context.\n\n`visibility: hidden` — different semantic: element occupies space, just invisible.\n\n`content-visibility` — CSS Containment level 2.\n\n`@media`-conditional `display: none` — at-rules deferred.\n\n## Next\n\nOnce ADR-017 merges, the implementation issue will be \"Implement display: none per ADR-017\" — one commit (UA rules + layout wiring + delete helper + tests). Then future \"this element doesn't render\" cases become UA stylesheet changes, not C++ changes.\n",
